      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "stock / format / medium: film stock, film size, print or digital output.\nparams.ev / temperature / tint: input light and white balance.\nparams.highlights / shadows / saturation / vibrance: color grade.\nparams.grain / profile.halation: texture and highlight glow.\nprofile.screenGrade / screenExposure: screen/print response.\n\nThese are parameters of ONE physical Fotufilm develop, not multiple stacked film passes. Presets in this folder are interchangeable JSON recipes."
      ],
      "title": "Recipe map",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        880,
        2830
      ],
      "size": [
        740,
        500
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 36,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "This grading-only graph contains no LTX nodes. Enter the saved master ZIP filename above, adjust the recipe, then run on the compatible GPU execution target. The optional original-SDR branch stays muted.\n\nRe-running the grade does not invoke LTX. Use mp4 first; change format to hlg for HDR delivery. The included Ektachrome E100 / screen / reference-exposure recipe supports HLG. Negative/print looks must export SDR.\n\nThe develop node already writes the result into ComfyUI/output. A second Save Video node is unnecessary. Direct ProRes assets in release 7 need the color-tag repair supplied by the app bridge; MP4 and HLG avoid that known limitation."
      ],
      "title": "Stage 2 \u00b7 reuse the master",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        1800,
        2660
      ],
      "size": [
        670,
        470
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 37,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Enable only when you want a film-treated original-SDR control. It uses the same recipe as group 08.\n\nMute groups 02\u201306 when comparing grades without reconstruction. Mute group 08 to render only this original-SDR branch. Unmuting both Fotufilm nodes renders both versions.\n\nFor the cleanest HDR investigation, set grain to 0 and leave exposure / highlights / shadows neutral. Change one parameter at a time. ComfyUI's ordinary canvas video preview is not a calibrated HDR monitor."
      ],
      "title": "Optional SDR control",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
  ],
